If you arrived from the caller's pre-evaluation validation failure, return there; otherwise proceed to Step 5.

## 5. Trigger Re-Evaluation

<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "DM a re-evaluation trigger to every dispatched evaluator (both DMs in a single message on Deep). The literal `RE_EVALUATE` marker wakes the evaluator's resume behavior — a free-form status DM with the same content does not. Give it the new HEAD SHA, the commit range, a plain account of what the wave changed and why, and anything the wave could *not* fix.\n",
  codex: "Re-engage every evaluator lane against the revised implementation. If an evaluator is still live, `send_message` it the re-evaluation context by its task path; if its task already completed, `resume_agent` it and send the same context — it resumes per its skill's \"When Resuming\" path. Only if re-engagement fails, `spawn_agent` a fresh child for that lane and inline its prior findings plus the re-evaluation context into the spawn `message`.\n",
  opencode: "Re-engage every evaluator lane against the revised implementation. If an evaluator is still live, `send_message` it the re-evaluation context by its task path; if its task already completed, `resume_agent` it and send the same context — it resumes per its skill's \"When Resuming\" path. Only if re-engagement fails, `spawn_agent` a fresh child for that lane and inline its prior findings plus the re-evaluation context into the spawn `message`.\n",
  antigravity: "DM a re-evaluation trigger to every dispatched evaluator (both DMs in a single message on Deep). The literal `RE_EVALUATE` marker wakes the evaluator's resume behavior — a free-form status DM with the same content does not. Give it the new HEAD SHA, the commit range, a plain account of what the wave changed and why, and anything the wave could *not* fix.\n"
}) %>
